  "notes": "{早|はや}まる is an intransitive verb ({自動詞|じどうし}). The transitive pair is {早|はや}める (to hasten, to bring forward).\n\nASPECT ({ている}):\n{早|はや}まっている can indicate an ongoing quickened state or a resulting change in timing.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {予定|よてい}が{早|はや}まる - schedule is moved earlier\n- {脈|みゃく}/{心拍|しんぱく}が{早|はや}まる - pulse/heartbeat quickens\n- {早|はや}まった{行動|こうどう} - hasty action\n- {早|はや}まるな - don't be hasty/rash\n\nUSAGE NOTE:\nIn the sense of \"being hasty,\" {早|はや}まる often carries a negative nuance, implying an impulsive or regrettable action.",
